<title>USA: Northwest Savings to merge with Corry.</title>
<headline>Northwest Savings to merge with Corry.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Pa. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest Savings Bank said Thursday it would merge with the mutually-owned Corry Savings Bank.</p>
<p>The company said it expected to close the deal, for which the banks will file an application with banking regulators shortly,  by the end of the year. Northwest officials were unavailable to provide details of the merger.</p>
<p>Northwest bought another savings bank, Bridgeville Savings Bank FSB, for $16 per share on February 21.</p>
